once again it's been a successful  fishing trip  despite the risks boxes upon boxes are  unloaded from the trawler and carefully  registered  the men are happy with the catch  especially with this delicacy  these are famous prime quality red  prawns  they don't come any larger the  mediterranean prawns are in great demand  in fine restaurants around  the world  in good times we earn 550 euro for a 12  kilo carton of prime quality red prawns  that works out as 45 euro per kilo  aboard this ship  the fishermen from mazara del vallo  spend weeks out at sea for such a catch  sometimes even up to two months but  they're taking a big risk  the richest fishing grounds in the  southern mediterranean are off the  libyan coast  in international waters but libya now  claims them as territorial waters  this has caused repeated conflicts like  in the summer of 2018  the libyan navy wanted to stop the  italian fishermen  and arrest the entire crew  in september that's exactly what  happened to marco moroney  his two trawlers were impounded by libya  the ship owner is in despair his 18 crew  members have been in a benghazi jail for  over three months fishermen have never  been held this long  not being able to see the ships the men  who work for me  that is awful it's like a sun that you  miss  who you can no longer hug  during that confrontation libyan  authorities pursued nine italian  trawlers on the open sea  unlike some of his colleagues captain  giuseppe giaccalone managed to get away  the libyans came close wanted to seize  all the captains and the ship papers  the trawlers were told to follow them  but we could flee  risking our lives the coast guard is  armed  they could have  back in 2018 the fishermen received help  italy sent a naval helicopter to aid the  trawlers  libyan speed boat was forced to back off  but now italy no longer provides such  protection in the southern mediterranean  off the libyan coast telling fishermen  such operations are too demanding and  politically sensitive  now they fish at their own peril  but we need protection so we can fish in  these international waters  otherwise what happened to the fishermen  will happen again  the ship owner has even spent two months  protesting outside the italian  parliament in rome  calling for his crew and fish trawlers  to be released  we are at risk of being arrested 74  nautical miles off the coast  because libya claims the open sea as its  territorial waters  europe and italy must take action  against this because this sea belongs to  nobody alone  it belongs to us all  that includes crew members like muhammad  he is one of six tunisians who worked on  the italian trawlers  who are now in jail in benghazi  muhammad's family is worried about him  in the past he was already arrested  twice by libya  but this time it's worse  in the past we were always in contact we  knew how he was doing  his phone always works this time we've  not heard from him in months  we have no idea what is going on or even  if he is still alive  whenever she can mohammed's daughter  nores meets the families of other  detained fishermen at the port of mazara  here they staged protests with ship  owner marco marone to give each other  hope  we're fighting for 18 italian fishermen  that includes six tunisians  two senegalese and two indonesians  all of them have lived here in masada  for many years  some of them even before i was born  the families have no choice the hunt for  the  lucrative red prawns must go on that is  the only thing that makes the fishing  industry in mazzara del vallo profitable  in international waters and that  includes off libya's coast  you
 

